/S /H3
/T (WHAT IS A MAJOR? A "major" within our belief system represents a doctrine or position that we consider fundamental to the historical understanding of Christianity. Examples of such majors include the exclusive nature of salvation through Jesus Christ, the inerrancy of Scripture, and the triune nature of God. These are non-negotiable principles, serving as foundational pillars on which the Church stands united and unwavering. )
/E (WHAT IS A MAJOR? A "major" within our belief system represents a doctrine or position that we consider fundamental to the historical understanding of Christianity. Examples of such majors include the exclusive nature of salvation through Jesus Christ, the inerrancy of Scripture, and the triune nature of God. These are non-negotiable principles, serving as foundational pillars on which the Church stands united and unwavering. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [20 21]
>>
