183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (WHAT IS A MINOR? A "minor" within our belief system refers to a doctrine or position that we uphold but do not consider essential enough to sever fellowship over. These are perspectives that we recognize as part of our faith tradition but do not deem crucial to the core understanding of Christianity. Examples of such minors include theological debates such as Calvinism versus Arminianism \(predestination versus free will\), variations in baptismal practices \(for further explanation, please refer to page 8\), and preferences regarding worship instrumentation.)
/E (WHAT IS A MINOR? A "minor" within our belief system refers to a doctrine or position that we uphold but do not consider essential enough to sever fellowship over. These are perspectives that we recognize as part of our faith tradition but do not deem crucial to the core understanding of Christianity. Examples of such minors include theological debates such as Calvinism versus Arminianism \(predestination versus free will\), variations in baptismal practices \(for further explanation, please refer to page 8\), and preferences regarding worship instrumentation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
